{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"Across 17 Genetech (Illumina distributor) reagent awards at Taiwan public buyers, the average award-to-budget ratio drifted down from about 89% (2023) to about 86% (2025-26). This is mild evidence of more discounting.","detail":"Award/budget ratios I computed from detail pages (reagent and consumable lots only, all single-bidder). 2023: CDC 2.299/2.420=95.0%, NTU 7.265/8.5475=85.0%, TVGH 6.67/7.25=92.0%, MOJ 0.287/0.3375=85.0%; mean 89.3%. 2024: CDC 2.29/2.5155=91.0%, NTU 4.92/5.799=84.9%, Vet institute 1.125/1.324=85.0%; mean 87.0%. 2025: CDC 10.18/12.32=82.6%, TVGH 3.942/4.635=85.0%, NTU 6.12/6.8=90.0%, Vet 1.246/1.467=84.9%; mean 85.6%. 2026: CDC 84.6%, NTUH 90.0%, TVGH P4/P3 87.9%/80.0%, MOJ 88.5%, Vet 83.4%; mean 85.7%. The drop is about 3.6 pts. Budgets are set by the buyer, so this measures negotiation off a ceiling, not list-price cuts. Samples are small and the lot mix changes.","url":"http://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=A.21.1&job_number=KA115051","date":"2023-2026","source_name":"Taiwan PCC award notices via pcc-api.openfun.app","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"This is a new pooled four-year award/budget series across buyers; prior items cite single awards."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"against","claim":"Illumina instrument sales through Genetech closed much closer to budget (about 94.5% on average) than reagent lots (about 86%), so instruments show less discounting than consumables.","detail":"Instrument award/budget: Chang Gung Linkou NT$2.245M/2.264M=99.2% (Aug 2025, 'ILLUMINA' brand in title, origin Singapore, 1 bidder after a failed first round); TFDA high-throughput system 5.6/5.8=96.6% (Apr 2025); Yunlin NTUH 5.05/5.35=94.4% (May 2025); Vet Research Institute 2.295/2.35=97.7% (May 2026, after one failed round); NTU upgrade 3.98/4.7=84.7% (Apr 2025). The mean is 94.5% against 86.3% for 7 reagent lots in 2026. Buyers accept near-ceiling prices on boxes, which fits a pricing model where Illumina earns on pull-through.","url":"http://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=43862061&job_number=0C-1L0324","date":"2025-04 to 2026-05","source_name":"Taiwan PCC award notices via pcc-api.openfun.app","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"The instrument-vs-reagent discount contrast is new; known items covered only reagent awards."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"Genetech's recurring NTU sequencer-reagent lot cost about 71% less per month of contract between 2023 and late 2025, the largest same-buyer fall in this file.","detail":"Lot 1124A012 (Jul 2023-Jun 2024): NT$7.265M over ~11.5 months, ~NT$0.63M/month. Lot 1134A016 (30 Sep 2024-Dec 2025): NT$4.92M over ~15 months, ~NT$0.33M/month (-48%). Lot 1142A007 (Oct 2025-Jul 2028): NT$6.12M over ~33 months, ~NT$0.185M/month (-71% vs 2023). All are single-bidder 'batch' lots with estimated quantities, so scope or volume changes could explain part of the drop. Direction is consistent with research buyers shifting NGS spend to other vendors or cheaper tiers. Treat it as a flag, not a price index.","url":"http://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=3.9.20&job_number=1142A007","date":"2023-07 to 2025-10","source_name":"Taiwan PCC award notices via pcc-api.openfun.app","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"NTU's repeating reagent lot has not been tracked before."},
{"label":"2A","direction":"supports","claim":"National Taiwan University (a research buyer) paid less per month for Illumina sample-prep and sequencing reagents with each renewal, and the 2025 lot was bargained to 90% of budget and 94.4% of floor.","detail":"The Oct 2025 award was NT$6,120,030 against a NT$6.8M budget, a NT$6,480,000 floor and a NT$6,799,990 winning bid (single bidder, MOST subsidy NT$5.44M). The price came in NT$359,970 below the floor. Even with one bidder, the buyer pushed 10% off the ceiling. The per-month trend is in the previous item.","url":"http://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=3.9.20&job_number=1142A007","date":"2025-10-30","source_name":"Taiwan PCC award notice 1142A007","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"The floor-price, bid and award gap at NTU has not been reported."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"Taipei VGH's two newest sole-bidder Illumina reagent awards landed 12% and 20% under item budgets. Its Nov 2025 HT lot was 15% under.","detail":"May 2026 P3 kit: 15 sets at NT$235,000 = NT$3.525M against a NT$4.406M budget (80.0%); the bid was NT$3.613M. Apr 2026 P4 kit: 18 sets at NT$201,000 = NT$3.618M against NT$4.1175M (87.9%); bid NT$4.1175M, i.e. the floor of NT$3.618M was the award. Nov 2025 HT reagent lot (4 bidders on the 7-item case) NT$3.942M vs NT$4.635M (85.0%), the winning bid equal to the budget. The Dec 2023 award was NT$6.67M vs NT$7.25M (92.0%). The unit prices (P4 201K, P3 235K) are already known; the new part is the budget gap and the bid-to-floor move.","url":"http://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=3.32.80&job_number=1150157V","date":"2026-04-29 to 2026-05-07","source_name":"Taiwan PCC award notices 1150157V, 1140732E, 1120652Y","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Unit prices are known; the budget-vs-award discount series and the first-round failure (22 Apr 2026) are new."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"The Taiwan CDC's NGS library-prep lot flatlined in 2026 after a 4.4x jump in 2025, so there is no further volume step-up at this buyer.","detail":"CDC annual lot: 2023 NT$2.299M (95% of budget), 2024 NT$2.29M (91%), 2025 NT$10.18M (82.6%, after a failed round on 6 Aug 2025), 2026 NT$10.199M (84.6%; budget 12.056M, down 2.2% from 12.322M). The 2026 award is +0.2% y/y against a 2.2% lower budget. The 4.4x scope step in 2025 was a one-time change; 2026 shows zero growth.","url":"http://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=A.21.1&job_number=KA114045","date":"2023-05 to 2026-09","source_name":"Taiwan PCC award notices HP112030, HP113021, KA114045, KA115051","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"The 4-year CDC series is new (known data cover only the 2026 award at about 1% above base)."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"Taiwan's Vet Research Institute still buys sequencing reagents in growing amounts, but its origin tag changed from US (2024) to Singapore (2025-26), which fits a move from a US-made legacy box to a Singapore-built newer Illumina box.","detail":"Library-prep reagent and chip lots: 2024 NT$1.125M (US origin, 85.0% of budget), 2025 NT$1.246M (Singapore, 84.9%), 2026 NT$1.595M (Singapore, 83.4%), i.e. +10.8% then +28%, with the discount to budget widening slightly. The institute also bought a NT$2.295M sequencer in May 2026 (Singapore origin). The origin shift is an inference about platform, not a stated product.","url":"http://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=A.19.13&job_number=115-2013","date":"2024-09 to 2026-10","source_name":"Taiwan PCC award notices B-113-0618, B-114-0880, 115-2013","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"The origin-country switch and 3-year series are new."},
{"label":"1B","direction":"supports","claim":"After a failed first round in Aug 2025, the Taiwan CDC's NT$12.3M library-prep tender was awarded to the only bidder at NT$10.18M, which is 17.4% under budget.","detail":"The 6 Aug 2025 round failed for too few bids. In the re-run (award 15 Aug 2025) the single bidder won at NT$10,180,000 against a NT$12,322,375 budget and NT$10,207,000 floor, i.e. 0.3% under the floor. The 2026 re-run followed the same pattern: floor NT$10.1M, award NT$10.199M, 15.4% under budget. A repeat 15-17% concession even without competition suggests the distributor prices off a known internal floor.","url":"http://pcc-api.openfun.app/api/tender?unit_id=A.21.1&job_number=KA114045","date":"2025-08-15","source_name":"Taiwan PCC award notice KA114045","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"Adds the floor-price and two-year pattern at the CDC."},
